---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.description}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
  bannerNotice={metadata.bannerNotice}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "1. Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "2. Scope" },
        { id: "s3", label: "3. Classification — Business Model and Cash Flow Characteristics" },
        { id: "s4", label: "4. The Three Measurement Categories" },
        { id: "s5", label: "5. The Equity Instrument FVOCI Election — No Recycling" },
        { id: "s6", label: "6. THE HEADLINE FEATURE — the Expected Credit Loss Model" },
        { id: "s7", label: "7. Why China Converged Years Ahead of Japan GAAP" },
        { id: "s8", label: "8. Worked Example — Classifying a Debt Instrument" },
        { id: "s9", label: "9. Worked Example — Recognising an Expected Credit Loss Allowance" },
        { id: "s10", label: "10. Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s11", label: "11. Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates" },
        { id: "s12", label: "12. Relationship to IFRS 9" },
        { id: "s13", label: "13. Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s14", label: "14. Related Standards" },
        { id: "s15", label: "15. Glossary" }
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="wrap">
</div>



<div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">A major, genuinely early convergence achievement</div><div class="principle">ASBE No. 22 governs the CLASSIFICATION, RECOGNITION, and MEASUREMENT of FINANCIAL instruments — REVISED in 2017 to REPLACE the OLDER, four-category CLASSIFICATION model (broadly RESEMBLING old IAS 39) with a MODERN, business-MODEL and cash-FLOW-characteristics-driven FRAMEWORK, INCLUDING a FORWARD-LOOKING expected CREDIT loss impairment MODEL — CLOSELY converged with IFRS 9 internationally, and NOTABLY AHEAD of comparable REFORMS in OTHER major jurisdictions (Section 7).</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Financial assets and financial liabilities</div><div class="principle">This Standard applies to the CLASSIFICATION and MEASUREMENT of FINANCIAL assets and FINANCIAL liabilities — WORKING alongside ASBE No. 23 (transfer of FINANCIAL assets), ASBE No. 24 (HEDGING), and ASBE No. 37 (PRESENTATION of financial INSTRUMENTS) to FORM the COMPLETE financial INSTRUMENTS framework.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Classification — Business Model and Cash Flow Characteristics</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">A two-part test, mirroring IFRS 9's own approach</div><div class="text-supporting">A DEBT financial ASSET is CLASSIFIED based on (a) the ENTITY'S business MODEL for MANAGING the asset (HOLD to COLLECT contractual CASH flows; HOLD to COLLECT and SELL; or OTHER), and (b) WHETHER the ASSET'S contractual CASH flows represent SOLELY payments of PRINCIPAL and INTEREST (the "SPPI" test) — CONSISTENT with IFRS 9'S OWN classification FRAMEWORK internationally.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>The Three Measurement Categories</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Amortised cost, FVOCI, and FVTPL</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;"><span>Category</span><span>Applies where</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;"><span>Amortised cost</span><span>HOLD-to-collect business MODEL, and CASH flows are SOLELY principal and INTEREST</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;"><span>Fair value through OCI (FVOCI)</span><span>HOLD-to-collect-and-SELL business MODEL, and cash FLOWS are SOLELY principal and INTEREST</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;"><span>Fair value through profit or loss (FVTPL)</span><span>ALL other financial ASSETS, INCLUDING those FAILING the SPPI test</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>The Equity Instrument FVOCI Election — No Recycling</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Retaining IFRS 9's own irrevocable no-recycling option</div><div class="text-supporting">CONSISTENT with UNMODIFIED IFRS 9 internationally, ASBE No. 22 PERMITS an IRREVOCABLE election to MEASURE certain EQUITY instruments at FVOCI, with FAIR value CHANGES NEVER recycled to PROFIT or loss, EVEN on DISPOSAL. NOTABLY, this is a POINT where ASBE DIFFERS from Japan'S JMIS Modification No. 2 (see the COMPANION poster EARLIER in this SERIES), WHICH specifically PROHIBITS this NO-recycling outcome — ASBE, UNLIKE JMIS, RETAINS the SAME "permanent PARKING" option unmodified IFRS 9 ALLOWS.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>THE HEADLINE FEATURE — the Expected Credit Loss Model</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Forward-looking loss estimation, replacing the old incurred-loss trigger</div><div class="text-supporting">The REVISED Standard REQUIRES recognising an ALLOWANCE for EXPECTED credit LOSSES — estimated BASED on FORWARD-looking information ABOUT future DEFAULT risk — RATHER than WAITING for a SPECIFIC, observable LOSS event (the OLD "incurred LOSS" trigger) BEFORE recognising IMPAIRMENT. This is the SAME fundamental SHIFT IFRS 9 introduced INTERNATIONALLY when it REPLACED IAS 39.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Why China Converged Years Ahead of Japan GAAP</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">A striking contrast within this comparative poster series</div><div class="text-supporting">CHINA'S REVISION to ASBE No. 22 — EFFECTIVE for LISTED companies from 2018 and OTHER enterprises from 2021 — TOOK effect ROUGHLY the SAME time as IFRS 9'S OWN international 2018 effective DATE. This STANDS in GENUINE contrast to Japan GAAP, WHOSE own financial INSTRUMENTS standard (ASBJ Statement No. 10) REMAINED anchored to an "OLD IAS 39"-style APPROACH for an EXTENDED period, ONLY proposing an EQUIVALENT expected CREDIT loss model via a FEBRUARY 2026 exposure DRAFT (see the COMPANION poster). This ILLUSTRATES how China'S explicit, ACTIVE "substantial CONVERGENCE" policy (discussed EARLIER when we FIRST began this SERIES) has PRODUCED genuinely FASTER alignment with CURRENT international STANDARDS in SOME areas, RELATIVE to other MAJOR Asian jurisdictions.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Worked Example — Classifying a Debt Instrument</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Applying the business model and SPPI tests</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: A corporate bond held to collect coupon and principal payments</div><div class="wk-body">A company purchases a corporate bond, intending to hold it to collect the contractual coupon and principal payments through to maturity. The bond's cash flows consist solely of fixed interest and principal repayment.</div><div class="wk-answer">Since the BUSINESS model is HOLD-to-collect and the CASH flows PASS the SPPI TEST, the bond is CLASSIFIED and MEASURED at <strong>AMORTISED COST</strong>.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Worked Example — Recognising an Expected Credit Loss Allowance</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">A forward-looking allowance, recognised before any default occurs</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: A trade receivable portfolio</div><div class="wk-body">A company holds RMB 200,000,000 of trade receivables measured at amortised cost, none currently in default, but historical and forward-looking data suggest an expected loss rate of 1.5%.</div><div class="wk-answer">The company recognises an EXPECTED credit LOSS allowance of RMB 200,000,000 × 1.5% = <strong>RMB 3,000,000</strong> — RECOGNISED EARLIER, and WITHOUT waiting for ANY confirmed DEFAULT event, REFLECTING the FORWARD-looking nature of the MODEL.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What ASBE No. 22 requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>Classification and carrying amounts of financial assets and liabilities, by category</span><span>Methodology and key assumptions used to estimate expected credit losses</span><span>Movement in the expected credit loss allowance during the period</span></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
<div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Determining the business model for managing a group of financial assets</span><span>Whether contractual cash flows pass the SPPI test</span></div></div>
<div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Forward-looking probability-weighted expected credit loss estimates</span></div></div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Relationship to IFRS 9</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — ASBE 22 vs IFRS 9</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Feature</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-warning);">ASBE 22</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-info);">IFRS 9</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Classification model</span><span>Business model + SPPI</span><span>Business model + SPPI — converged</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Impairment model</span><span>Expected credit loss</span><span>Expected credit loss — converged</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Equity FVOCI no-recycling election</span><span>Available</span><span>Available — converged</span></div>
</div>
<div class="note">ONE of the MOST thoroughly and PROMPTLY converged standards in the ENTIRE ASBE suite.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where every financial instrument event lands</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Expected credit loss allowance</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span> <span class="badge bp">IS</span></span><span>Recognised forward-looking, before default occurs</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Standard</span><span>Connection</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>ASBE No. 23</span><span>Transfer of Financial Assets — governs derecognition, complementing this Standard's classification and measurement scope</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>ASBE No. 24</span><span>Hedging — governs hedge accounting for instruments within this Standard's scope</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s15"><span class="num">15</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2">
<div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">SPPI test</div><div class="glossary-def">A test assessing whether a financial asset's contractual cash flows represent solely payments of principal and interest.</div></div>
<div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;"><div class="glossary-term">Expected credit loss (ECL)</div><div class="glossary-def">A forward-looking, probability-weighted estimate of credit losses, recognised before a specific loss event is confirmed.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="legend"><div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (Chinese GAAP / ASBE terminology)</div><div class="lrow"><div class="litem"><span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet (资产负债表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bp">IS</span> Income Statement (利润表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bo">SCOE</span> Statement of Changes in Owners' Equity (所有者权益变动表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bc">CFS</span> Cash Flow Statement (现金流量表)</div></div></div>


</div>
  </div>
  <section id="history">
    <HistoryTimeline items={history.asbe22 || []} />
  </section>
</StandardPageLayout>
